6-11-05T05:14:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T05:03:46Z","closed_at":"2026-11-13T09:02:13Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Part of the worlds design program: [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955). Wave-2 follow-up from the prior-art research (Lane B item 45); parent topic issue: [#5989](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5989). Research source: `workspace/scratch/worlds-capabilities-brief-2026-11-04/prior-art-research.md`.\n\n## State of the art (2025)\n\nGoblins (Guile + Racket; Hoot compiles to WebAssembly) models objects in **vats** processing transactional **turns**, with promise pipelining and distributed GC; *The Heart of Spritely* (May 2025) is the canonical design doc (https://spritely.institute/static/papers/spritely-core.pdf). **OCapN** is the cross-implementation protocol suite: **CapTP** for capability-preserving remote invocation over pluggable netlayers, references as unforgeable sturdyrefs (`ocapn://…`). **Caveat in Spritely's own docs: CapTP support \"is still in its early days — do not rely on the protocol being stable\"** (https://files.spritely.institute/docs/guile-goblins/0.13.0/OCapN.html).\n\n## Position for id (from the research)\n\n**Dead end for now:** adopting OCapN as id's wire protocol in v1. Adopt the *discipline* (no ambient authority; authority travels by reference passing) — which Roc already enforces one level down by platform exclusivity and explicit context passing — design handle semantics to be OCapN-*compatible*, and revisit when CapTP stabilizes.\n\n## Work\n\n- Watch: re-check CapTP/OCapN stability status on a cadence; record dated state changes here.\n- Spike (when the watch says it's worth it): a minimal CapTP interop test between a Goblins vat and an id-side stub — feasibility evidence before any v2 commitment.\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA dated watch log plus, when triggered, a spike report with a go/no-go for bridge work.\n","closed_by":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/